ssageBody":"","tags":["A-Checkstyle"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":69,"deletions":4}}}]},{"date":"2026-09-08T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"ad8cf82e724bc2779a4730a263401e344cfc144d","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Tighten parser validation","messageBody":"This change makes input validation fail fast for invalid task numbers and isolates the event and deadline parsing details into small helper methods. The result is clearer command parsing, lower risk of index errors, and code that is easier to maintain in line with the course\u0027s code-quality guidance.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":80,"deletions":63}}},{"hash":"e6c0297829c0ae5aa947fa46aaeb1f2877239a1b","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Refactor storage parsing helpers","messageBody":"This change follows the code-quality guidance to keep methods short, avoid deep nesting, and extract repeated parsing and formatting concerns into focused helpers. It also replaces magic task-type literals with named constants so the persistence layer is easier to read, review, and modify without introducing subtle bugs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot \u003c223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":166,"deletions":65}}},{"hash":"ddffeeb4db4b3ad5109a37f7fe1014910e78fcd8","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix Checkstyle indentation","messageBody":"This patch aligns switch-case blocks with the project’s Checkstyle rules so the code remains consistent with the course’s formatting guidance. The changes are intentionally small and mechanical: they keep the logic unchanged while correcting indentation to make the code easier to read and maintain.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot \u003c223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":41,"deletions":41}}},{"hash":"9869b4c65d7ec9a5e4c302d1ba1425c153cd5a76","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Rename storage tests to project convention","messageBody":"This patch updates the new storage test names to follow the repository’s required method-naming convention. The intent is to keep test names explicit and consistent with the rest of the suite so future failures are easier to understand and review.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot \u003c223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":2,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"77837ed0424a49bddd017449e1fccaa09a0f2ea4","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #1 from FrancisRalph/branch-A-CodeQuality","messageBody":"Branch a code quality","tags":["A-CodeQuality"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"a9e4348796efc954d6a26aff603714a16e07dce9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add assertions to document invariants","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":13,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"175feb25232f702f5a38067766eb4f171647eb32","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #2 from FrancisRalph/branch-A-Assertions","messageBody":"Add assertions to document invariants","tags":["A-Assertions"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"be5f3ee0076ce69c1770f4532f57efcefe251c3b","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Implement in-memory sorting for list command","messageBody":"Support \u0027list /by deadline\u0027 and \u0027list /by status\u0027 by adding TaskList.getAllSorted that returns a stable, in-memory sorted view. The ListCommand and CommandHandler were updated to accept an optional \u0027/by \u003ckey\u003e\u0027 argument and delegate to the new method. Invalid sort keys throw RalphException. Added unit tests for sorting behavior and stability. No storage or persisted format changes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot \u003c223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n","tags":["A-FullCommitMessage"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":210,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"9d6579fe178f4548a359c4d342987a5b8102c4b0","isMergeCommit":true,"messa